TI  - Candida albicans endophthalmitis in a patient with a non-functioning pituitary 
      adenoma evolving into Cushing׳s disease: A case report.
PG  - 37-41
LID - 10.1016/j.mmcr.2014.09.001 [doi]
AB  - A 53-year-old woman presented with complaints of blurred vision in the left eye. 
      She had been treated for recurrent non-functioning pituitary adenoma (NFPA). A 
      vitreous biopsy followed by histopathologic examination showed the presence of 
      Candida albicans. Meanwhile, Cushing׳s disease was diagnosed and gamma knife 
      surgery was performed. Vitrectomy and antifungal treatment improved ocular 
      infection and inflammation. Herein, we describe the first case of C. albicans 
      endophthalmitis in a patient with NFPA evolving into Cushing׳s disease.
