DP  - 1989 Jun
TI  - Variations in red blood cell polyamines in brain tumour patients treated with 
      stereotactic radiosurgery.
PG  - 76-8
AB  - Red blood cell polyamine levels were followed in 13 patients treated with 
      stereotactic radiosurgery for various types of brain tumours. In the most 
      malignant tumours radiosurgery resulted in a decrease in spermine and an increase 
      in spermidine levels. This discrepancy between variations in polyamine levels was 
      not found after conventional radiotherapy. The results may indicate a change in 
      tumour polyamine activity induced by high energy radiotherapy.
