VI  - 76
IP  - 1-2
DP  - 1985
TI  - Tumour ploidy in DNA histograms of pituitary adenomas.
PG  - 18-22
AB  - DNA analysis was performed by flow cytometry (FCM) in 59 cases of different types 
      of pituitary adenomas who underwent microsurgery and were actively followed over 
      a period of 3-6 years. Aneuploid DNA patterns were detected in 12 (20%) cases. 
      Frequency of aneuploidy was highest in prolactin-secreting (36%) as compared to 
      17% in GH- and 7% in non-secreting adenomas. Some adenoma parameters valid for 
      tumour growth, such as rate of recurrences and mitotic index, were correlated 
      with aneuploidy of the tumour. FCM studies are, therefore, recommended to gain 
      further parameters for the estimation of proliferative activity of pituitary 
      adenomas.
